{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/846442-pacts-and-pledges","id":846442,"title":"Pacts and Pledges","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-03-12T22:03:05-08:00","id":846442,"title":"Pacts and Pledges","content":"Im curious as to why pledges are being changed from how they worked in 1st edition. i like sealing, and the other added benefits from pledges, but some of my favourite moments playing changeling are when characters or npcs trap each other with binding word play. I know demon modeled their pacts after 1st edition changeling, and am curious as to why changeling is itself changing the model.<br /> <br /> I know goblin vows are the new* form of old pledges, so you're able to keep the min maxing, or the flexibility of buffs, like the 1st editions pledges, I just find most of the charm of it is removed, as it removes some of the roleplayed interactions between two parties, providing things for one another for bonuses.<br /> <br /> so if I ask, why the change/removal of the old pledge system? I'm gonna miss people bringing my character cookies(and glamour) for boons.<br /> <br /> <br /> *goblin vows working the same way in 1st edition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1377-wrequis","name":"Wrequis","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"111"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-12T22:08:44-08:00","id":846446,"title":"","content":"Because the old one was broken and clunky? This one allows for quicker gameplay that mirrors folklore more closely. No finagling numbers, you just take the words and <i>go</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-12T22:23:35-08:00","id":846452,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wrequis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/846442-pacts-and-pledges#post846442\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just find most of the charm of it is removed, as it removes some of the roleplayed interactions between two parties, providing things for one another for bonuses.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know about you, but when over sixty percent of the pagespace allotted to any given pledge is talking about its boons and sanctions and a disgusting proportion of hypothetically-constructed pledges people came up with didn't even bother with wording, I don't have much faith in the mechanics' ability to model tricksy fairy word-bond magic with concision, much less charm.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-12T22:47:35-08:00","id":846461,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/846442-pacts-and-pledges?p=846446#post846446\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because the old one was broken and clunky? This one allows for quicker gameplay that mirrors folklore more closely. No finagling numbers, you just take the words and <i>go</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> you always answer me with questions im finding lol.<br /> <br /> anyways, i found once the rules were known enough, my players and I would throw pledges left right and center, and you really had to watch what you said around changelings, just sad to see that extra level of paranoia taken out<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1377-wrequis","name":"Wrequis","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"111"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-12T23:03:27-08:00","id":846466,"title":"","content":"if you pose someone a question, like 'can you pick up x person from y place?' and they say 'sure', can you seal them? or do they have to actually state 'I will pick up x person at y place' to seal them?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1377-wrequis","name":"Wrequis","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"111"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-12T23:13:16-08:00","id":846467,"title":"","content":"Sure is enough of a commitment.<br /> <br /> As for the First Edition Pledges-Look, I've spent nearly nine years on being the Changeling Guy. I could spit out the words for a pledge easy as crap, but even i basically just said &quot;Fuck the mechanics of it, we'll finagle it when we take a pause unless it somehow hits the same scene, in which case we'll wing the entire thing.&quot;<br /> <br /> Not to mention that Pledges were so damn powerful, they broke the game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-12T23:26:33-08:00","id":846471,"title":"","content":"Yeah I can definitely see that, and im glad to see someone else with pledge-fu!<br /> <br /> also,. Know if you see me asking questions, it isn't me crying about things being removed, added, or changed, its really me curiously wondering why x changes take place, as, i trust you guys with this game, and everything thusfar is awesome.<br /> <br /> with that in mind, how do you see goblin vows being less powerful, or game breaking than 1st edition pledges? they seem to work mostly the same, and are just harder to establish with requiring a medium","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1377-wrequis","name":"Wrequis","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"111"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-12T23:32:28-08:00","id":846473,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wrequis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/846442-pacts-and-pledges?p=846471#post846471\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">with that in mind, how do you see goblin vows being less powerful, or game breaking than 1st edition pledges? they seem to work mostly the same, and are just harder to establish with requiring a medium</div> </div> </div> </div>Goblin vows are explicitly limited by purview and are closest in 2e's pledge mechanics to particularly high-stakes unbreakable Sealings, with all the punitive costs of forswearing that implies. 1e's pledges, as was often observed, could give you functionally anything by pledging with literally anyone.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-13T01:50:29-08:00","id":846500,"title":"","content":"The new Pledge system is an awesome framework, I much prefer it to 1E.<br /> <br /> It just needs more powerful effects, breaking a Pledge should be bad enough that The Milliner's Daughter would seriously consider giving Rumplestiltskin her baby out of fear of the consequences. Or to put it another way, there's specific mechanics for Sealing a Huntsman, if a Changeling is crafty and canny and Seals the Huntsman into giving up his hunt that should be the end of the Huntsman (either permanently or until the Huntsman return to Arcadian ephemera frees it from all pledges. Either works.) But if I was playing a Huntsman, I'd just take the point of Lethal damage and carry on hunting. If it's mechanically optimal for a fae creature to break a bargain then you know Pledges are underpowered.<br /> <br /> Oaths would probably be fine if benefits were per Scene or Session rather than Chapter. Bargains would be fine, though upping the penalty to -2 wouldn't hurt, if there were specific places that the Hunstman rolls; but I worry that if a Storyteller introduces Huntsmen whenever they're dramatically appropriate then it might be a penalty to a roll that never occurs. I wouldn't say no to different kinds of Bargain either. So instead of protection from Huntsman you might get Status in a mortal institution, or the Alternate Identity Merit. Etc<br /> <br /> <br /> So basically. I love the design of the new system, but the mechanical potency of 2E Pledges could use a boost.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-13T03:04:47-07:00","id":846501,"title":"","content":"Unrelated side question: can a fae creature break his word regarding a pledge, by his own choice rather than accident, in the new version?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","name":"Raistlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-13T05:16:30-07:00","id":846530,"title":"","content":"Yes. If they break a Sealing they get the stronger (but still rather weak) penalty without a Changeling having to invest extra in the Sealing. If they break an Oath they gain the Oathbreaker Condition (major social penalties with all fae) but other than that they IIRC get no additional penalties from the Wyrd.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-13T12:03:54-07:00","id":846663,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/846442-pacts-and-pledges?p=846530#post846530\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes. If they break a Sealing they get the stronger (but still rather weak) penalty without a Changeling having to invest extra in the Sealing. If they break an Oath they gain the Oathbreaker Condition (major social penalties with all fae) but other than that they IIRC get no additional penalties from the Wyrd.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Crap! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> one of the few advantages changelings used to have over Gentry is the possibility of deliberately breaking a pledge (even if risky and harmful, sometimes is better than the alternative), which it was as impossible for a True Fae as for us to break a physic law.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","name":"Raistlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-13T12:16:55-07:00","id":846669,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Raistlin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/846442-pacts-and-pledges?p=846663#post846663\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Crap! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> one of the few advantages changelings used to have over Gentry is the possibility of deliberately breaking a pledge (even if risky and harmful, sometimes is better than the alternative), which it was as impossible for a True Fae as for us to break a physic law.</div> </div> </div> </div>Incorrect. The Fae are as disinclined to break pledges as anyone else who knows what the consequences of doing so are, but the only sense in which that Gentry find it &quot;impossible&quot; to deliberately break a pledge is that some of the things they can swear one on include their limbs and their lives.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-13T13:15:18-07:00","id":846697,"title":"","content":"Is that in the books? I always thought that the True Fae didn't break Pledges.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-13T13:29:21-07:00","id":846708,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/846442-pacts-and-pledges?p=846697#post846697\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is that in the books? I always thought that the True Fae didn't break Pledges.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Don't usually, at least on purpose&quot; is markedly distinct from &quot;Cannot,&quot; and the latter is reserved for promises they've staked their continued existence on. The Fae have to stumble into breaking a Namebound oath, whether through trickery or carelessness.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-13T13:45:37-07:00","id":846711,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/846442-pacts-and-pledges?p=846467#post846467\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sure is enough of a commitment.<br /> <br /> As for the First Edition Pledges-Look, I've spent nearly nine years on being the Changeling Guy. I could spit out the words for a pledge easy as crap, but even i basically just said &amp;quot;Fuck the mechanics of it, we'll finagle it when we take a pause unless it somehow hits the same scene, in which case we'll wing the entire thing.&amp;quot;<br /> <br /> Not to mention that Pledges were so damn powerful, they broke the game.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just echoing that this is more or less my experience well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-13T14:34:54-07:00","id":846723,"title":"","content":"I don't even think it was that they were powerful so much as the mechanics made them supremely exploitable. The zero sum system allowed for Herculean tasks with minimal punishment for failure to still give massive buffs, among other issues.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-13T20:03:34-07:00","id":846886,"title":"","content":"No True Fae can break pledges in 1e and suffer the consquences, which if its a pledge on a True Faecs titles is like cutting off ones own limb for breaking it, and if its on theTrue Fae name, breaking the pledge kills the True Fae completely.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-13T21:23:19-07:00","id":846924,"title":"","content":"Here are my thoughts on pledges.<br /> <br /> My first impression was that plddges had gotten beaten hard and put away wet by the nerf stick.<br /> <br /> This was a mix of misreading it and not having the key info on goblin vows.<br /> <br /> The weak verison sealings can be very powerful when used right. If one keys to the right sort of promise, tricked out of the target usually, one could sabotage an assassination attempt, cock block someone, at a key moment, a small trick that could have huge implications depending upon the timing.<br /> <br /> If some promises never to drive on black ice, then does and takes a plenty to driving skill, you could get them killed.<br /> <br /> If used frivilously then yeah, its usually going to be a minor annoyance unless the target is really unluckly, but with the right timing, it could be deadly.<br /> <br /> Even the minor supernatural effect could be deadly, especially if your being hunted by well Hunters, and they see this tell that your reflection went weird for no reason. Possibly other things depending on how creative and generous one is with the definition of minor (I'd say minor is anything that wouldn't directly require rolling or dealing damage, or long lasting, no mechanical effect, although that doesn't mean no conquences).<br /> <br /> Then you have the strong sealing and most of the above is even more true for Strong Sealings naturally enough.<br /> <br /> But the key difference isn't the choice of lethal damage, which will only be a major issue when close to death or unconsciousness.<br /> <br /> No the big daddy is the ability to unleash a contract on the sealing breaker.<br /> <br /> Possible effects include Luna's Bedlam, Paraylyizing Shudder, the various contracts that deal or risk clarity damage, Terrible Harvest, The Fairest Effect verison of Phantom Glory, in some cases Pipes of the Beast Caller, Creeping Dread, Changeling Fate, Know the Competetion, Mask of Supierority, Read Lucidity, Murkblur, Flickering Hours, Portents and Visions, Riddle Kith, Shared Burden, Temporary Lucidity, Fairest Effect of Hidden Reality, Leaping Towards Nightfall, Thief of Reason, Tying the Knots of Fate.<br /> <br /> At the right time unleashing most of theses on someone can be brutal.<br /> <br /> But here is the twist, for a handful of them you can REWARD someone for breaking a sealing.<br /> <br /> Example a loved one promises to never allow themselves to come close to death by violence, accident, or disease and you seal their promise, strengthen its and here's the kicker, you tie the contract Shared Burden to it.<br /> <br /> They break that promise by getting cancer or AIDS and Shared Burden activates and heals them for example. <br /> <br /> Another example person X promises never to get into a fight, you seal the promise, strengthen it, and tie it to a use of Phantom Glory with both the Fairest and Elemental Effects and now next time they get into a fight you basically gave them a superpower, the ability to turn into the Human Tourch or Thing from the fantastic four (abit only for one fight, but still cool).<br /> <br /> I don't think this twist was intended.<br /> <br /> Bargains could be more exciting and should grant glamour to the changeling each time they are kept (with none fae or fae touched only).<br /> <br /> Oaths are kind of cool, could be stronger, but weirdly forever so Changeling would rarely want to give them. Also given how the court oath works, a court goodwill oath makes sense as well (instead of getting a dot of Mantle, you get a dot of Court Goodwill by pledging to be a loyal ally.)<br /> <br /> Goblin Vows got all the best stuff. Its a mix of nerf and buff. Only being able to make deals in reguards to the purview of the goblin vows you have narrows ones choices, but not by a alot.<br /> <br /> What's bigger is that you can make direct deals between people like in 1e Changeling and this doesn't change that. So you can't grant a mortal say resources \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 anymore in exchange for services to you (you might be able to seal said mortals words to the wyrd instead of yourself, effectively granting the mortal the use of your goblin vow and grant him or her say \u2022\u2022\u2022 resources at most).<br /> <br /> But flip side of that is you can at least grant yourself magical merits and contracts now, which you could do before.<br /> <br /> This means you can gain alot of powerful effects from say Riddle Kith \u2022\u2022\u2022 contract (aka the gift that keeps on giving), a longer life or even immortality with long of days merit, a hedge beast companion, a Fae Mount, a giant hollow filled with Luxuries (Hollow size \u2022\u2022 can be the size of a town or castle, + Luxuries is Hollow \u2022), Dual Kith, or you could go even weirder into stuff Changelings technically qualify for like Sleepwalker Merits from Mage.<br /> <br /> Or you could magically enhance yourself at everything you do for +3 dice, buff your basic abilities for up to +5, or basically master a skill for +7, which while it only effects your rolls, will in practice make you a major master of that skill.<br /> <br /> So if you pick Crafts and gain the +7 dice to all crafts rolls, your being to be awsome at carpntery, plumping, metallurgy, Dreamweaving, Hedgespinning, contracts that require a crafts roll, ect...<br /> <br /> So in that sense its both narrower and tighter, but also more fantastic and powerful.<br /> <br /> Its also interesting that all Fae (abit Fae Touched only partially, and Fetches not at all) can use pledges. So your Incubi, Succubi, Hedge Beasts, Changelings, Huntsmen, True Fae, various hobgoblins, Cambions, and who knows what else can make pledges.<br /> <br /> And if they can make pledges they can do things like join your motley (well normally only loyalists would invite a Huntsmen to join their motley), join a Changeling Court, which means they can get access to goblin vows, and so on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-13T21:41:33-07:00","id":846928,"title":"","content":"Correction: Reread the section on Oaths and only Changelings and (and if one reads the Fae Touchef section) the Fae Touched can join an Oath.<br /> <br /> But The rest of the Fae as far as I can tell can all use Sealings and Bargains.<br /> <br /> Goblin Vows are a maybe, they seem to be a specialized form of sealing with aspects of the wyrd.<br /> <br /> And one thing that is meantioned in the Dreamwalking section not the pledge section is that having a pledge with someone means you can cross in and out of their Bastion without having to roll.<br /> <br /> Which makes pledges, even the most pointless Sealings or dull Bargains useful for getting easy enterance into someones dreams. They're a free pass, aka a VIP or Membership card.<br /> <br /> Just a interesting thought, but given that oaths are forever, it'd be cool if it was possible to make an oath with a human, but it turned them into a Fae Touched. Just an idea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-13T21:56:24-07:00","id":846936,"title":"","content":"One thing left out is how someone ensorcells a mortal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-14T05:43:24-07:00","id":847026,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/846442-pacts-and-pledges?p=846936#post846936\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One thing left out is how someone ensorcells a mortal.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> yeah im really curious how this works.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1377-wrequis","name":"Wrequis","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"111"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-14T08:17:41-07:00","id":847089,"title":"","content":"You can sort of do it by dropping your mask in front of them, but there's a few drawbacks with that method.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-14T09:13:10-07:00","id":847117,"title":"","content":"Bewitched condition appears to be an odd sort of ensorcelled.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-14T09:32:33-07:00","id":847134,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/846442-pacts-and-pledges?p=846500#post846500\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So basically. I love the design of the new system, but the mechanical potency of 2E Pledges could use a boost.</div> </div> </div> </div>How bad would it be to upgrade it from 1 Lethal to 1 permanent/persistent Health reduction? Survivable in the short term, but such consequences can really add up over time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-14T09:56:47-07:00","id":847152,"title":"","content":"I'd prefer something like a permement condition like loosing an arm or loosing the ability to walk. In actual fairy tales it's usually a one pledge deal.<br /> <br /> In The Three Spinning Women the protagonist keeps her pledge and is greatly rewarded for it.<br /> <br /> In Bluebeard the protagonist breaks her word and dies.<br /> <br /> So even an individual pledge should be a big deal like that. Maybe not death, (to be fair, under 1E rules Bluebeard would have used a sanction of Vulnerability not Death). There should be at least one sanction that can neutralise a Huntsman, because if there's rules for Sealing a Hunstman (and there are) it should be 1) Hard to do. 2) Completely defeat the Hunstman if done successfully - even if the True Fae can just summon it again later.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/846442-pacts-and-pledges?p=846924#post846924\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The weak verison sealings can be very powerful when used right. If one keys to the right sort of promise, tricked out of the target usually, one could sabotage an assassination attempt, cock block someone, at a key moment, a small trick that could have huge implications depending upon the timing.</div> </div> </div> </div> That's the thing. In actual fairy tales there is no &quot;depending upon the timing&quot;. If there's a fairy tale about a Pledge it's <i>always</i> vitally important. Usually it's the core of the entire story. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/846442-pacts-and-pledges?p=846924#post846924\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But here is the twist, for a handful of them you can REWARD someone for breaking a sealing.</div> </div> </div> </div> Fairy tale and rewarded for breaking a pledge are two concepts that should never be used togeather.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-18T19:32:05-07:00","id":849573,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/846442-pacts-and-pledges?p=847152#post847152\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd prefer something like a permement condition like loosing an arm or loosing the ability to walk. In actual fairy tales it's usually a one pledge deal.<br /> <br /> In The Three Spinning Women the protagonist keeps her pledge and is greatly rewarded for it.<br /> <br /> In Bluebeard the protagonist breaks her word and dies.<br /> <br /> So even an individual pledge should be a big deal like that. Maybe not death, (to be fair, under 1E rules Bluebeard would have used a sanction of Vulnerability not Death). There should be at least one sanction that can neutralise a Huntsman, because if there's rules for Sealing a Hunstman (and there are) it should be 1) Hard to do. 2) Completely defeat the Hunstman if done successfully - even if the True Fae can just summon it again later.<br /> <br /> That's the thing. In actual fairy tales there is no &amp;quot;depending upon the timing&amp;quot;. If there's a fairy tale about a Pledge it's <i>always</i> vitally important. Usually it's the core of the entire story. <br /> <br /> Fairy tale and rewarded for breaking a pledge are two concepts that should never be used togeather.</div> </div> </div> </div> I get that but its still in the rules. Maybe I'd refluff those particular Sealings so that instead of being all stick, they all honey.<br /> <br /> Like instead of sealing a promise not to eat cheetos, and punish the sealing with a negative contract unleashed upon them, have a positive sealing where say they promise not to eat a cheetos till they go see a dietician about they're health, they are rewarded by gaining the benifit of a positively used contract, like Shared Burden.<br /> <br /> You could expand the Sealings to work that way. Negative Sealings punish promise breakers, and Positive Sealings reward promise Keepers.<br /> <br /> Just an idea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-19T00:53:32-07:00","id":849639,"title":"","content":"I'd be fine with Sealings having the ability to automatically invoke a positive contract if the other guy fulfils their end of the deal. I would quite like them to require a roughly equivalent curse if they break their word though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 03-19-2016, 04:40 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-19T10:48:08-07:00","id":849794,"title":"","content":"Considering that a Sealing being fulfilled is its own reward (whether in practical results, in trust, or in avoiding a consequence) when they're not purposely worded to entrap, I don't think they need benefits like that. And more severe curses don't quite feel appropriate as a punishment relative to the ease with which they can made.<br /> <br /> It'd be nice to have some form of personal faerie promise that could give direct rewards, but Sealings aren't the place for it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":188,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","user":"YeOfLittleFaith","date":". 03-19-2016, 02:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-20T18:09:38-07:00","id":850346,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>YeOfLittleFaith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/846442-pacts-and-pledges?p=849794#post849794\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Considering that a Sealing being fulfilled is its own reward (whether in practical results, in trust, or in avoiding a consequence) when they're not purposely worded to entrap, I don't think they need benefits like that. And more severe curses don't quite feel appropriate as a punishment relative to the ease with which they can made.<br /> <br /> It'd be nice to have some form of personal faerie promise that could give direct rewards, but Sealings aren't the place for it.</div> </div> </div> </div> There are goblin vows, but its vague on if you can seal someone else's promise to a goblin vow.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}